# /sdd-drift

Purpose:
  Detect drift between .sdd declarations and observed reality across
  all drift types.

Owns: commands/sdd-drift.sdd

Description:
  Compares declared architecture, behavior, contracts, database schema,
  security policies, configuration, documentation, and terminology
  against code, tests, DB, API, and infra. Produces drift records with
  classification and evidence.

Usage:
  /sdd-drift
  /sdd-drift --type <structural|behavioral|contract|database|security|configuration|documentation|terminology>
  /sdd-drift --scope <project|module|file>
  /sdd-drift --severity <HIGH|MEDIUM|LOW>
  /sdd-drift --json

Options:
  --type       Filter by drift type
  --scope      Analyze specific project, module, or file path
  --severity   Minimum severity to report
  --json       Output machine-readable JSON

Mode: READ_ONLY

Output:
  DRIFT REPORT

    Total Drifts:    <n>
    By Type:
      Structural:    <n>
      Behavioral:    <n>
      Contract:      <n>
      Database:      <n>
      Security:      <n>
      Configuration: <n>
      Documentation: <n>
      Terminology:   <n>
    By Classification:
      Declaration Wrong: <n>
      Code Wrong:        <n>
      Both Outdated:     <n>
      Unknown:           <n>
    Decision:         PASS | BLOCK | WARN

  Items:
    [D<id>] <type> | <classification> | <confidence>
      Declared: <sdd excerpt>
      Observed: <code/runtime excerpt>
      Evidence: [<ids>]
      Sync:     <SYNC_SDD | SYNC_CODE | SYNC_BOTH | REVIEW>

Rules:
  [DRF-01] /sdd-drift MUST classify every drift before reporting.
  [DRF-02] /sdd-drift MUST include evidence for every finding.
  [DRF-03] /sdd-drift MUST NOT silently ignore UNKNOWN drifts.
  [DRF-04] /sdd-drift MUST respect source-of-truth declarations.

Navigation:
